/pull/101308#issuecomment-2578831742","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101308","id":2578831742,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Ztdl-","user":{"login":"granitrocky","id":5321817,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMjE4MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5321817?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky","html_url":"https://github.com/granitrocky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-08T22:52:30Z","updated_at":"2025-01-08T22:52:30Z","body":"The use case is the same as for the linked ESCN exporter. Any place you would use that option, you would use this option.\r\n\r\nIt lets you simply give a name in blender for the material, and the importer automatically grabs that material and applies it to the mesh in godot.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2578831742/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2578976307","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101308#issuecomment-2578976307","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101308","id":2578976307,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZuA4z","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T00:51:26Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T00:51:26Z","body":"Feature [makes sense to me](https://x.com/passivestar_/status/1810861237795786839), haven't tested","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2578976307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579944925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101308#issuecomment-2579944925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101308","id":2579944925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZxtXd","user":{"login":"granitrocky","id":5321817,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMjE4MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5321817?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky","html_url":"https://github.com/granitrocky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T11:41:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T11:41:49Z","body":"> the other thing that would make this behavior more obvious is if the material name contains the full res:// path rather than guessing.\r\n\r\nIs there a more idiomatic way to get a resource file based solely on its name? the Material name in blender would be something like `Assets/Shaders/MaterialA`, and this code would try to find that file using that path.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579944925/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580126348","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101308#issuecomment-2580126348","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101308","id":2580126348,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZyZqM","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T13:14:11Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T13:23:18Z","body":"The Idiomatic to search for a resource by name could be to literally look for something with a matching name, not a semi-absolute path (for example, it is common to have rules like search for material/filename and simply filename recursively up). However, this will cause inconsistent imports if files are later renamed.\r\n\r\nif the idea to be an absolute project path then wouldn't the idiomatic way to reference an absolute resource path in Godot be with res://\r\n\r\nstill, I think this will add complexity in parts of the import system I am not comfortable with. For example, the advanced importer will now have three modes: embedded gltf material; project path by material name; and extracted material.\r\n\r\nAnd the other problem is while we are trying to add support for UID references, these materiqls won't be compatible with UID. Overall, I feel this system is a step backwards.\r\n\r\nAnother thing I want to note, if this workflow is of interest, it is possible to implement mapping the materials to filesystem paths as a post-import plugin without needing to change the core importer.\r\n\r\nedit: just a note to acknowledge the escn material search is a blender *exporter* feature. It does allow configuring names and absolute paths. (the paths are baked in during the export flow), I do see some value in this workflow, but I just don't think modifying the gltf importer is the right way given how it is likely to conflict with the material extraction feature","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580126348/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580181884","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101308#issuecomment-2580181884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101308","id":2580181884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZynN8","user":{"login":"granitrocky","id":5321817,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMjE4MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5321817?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky","html_url":"https://github.com/granitrocky","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/granitrocky/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T13:37:04Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T13:37:04Z","body":"@lyuma  All totally valid points. Could you expand a bit on the new UID system or point me to a spot where that is documented? ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2580181884/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]